#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175190 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sin 2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175190 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175190 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fc745be2-92c7-52a4-8ad3-491f01df1355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175191 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175191 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175191 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0bce1fbe-47f6-5c47-9ba0-df4ac06ddac9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186175199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186175200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186175201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186175202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186175203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175198 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c82a5a11-516b-565e-a445-ea24ede32e57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175199 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175199 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175199 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "814f7c9d-5e49-5f4e-b1de-405ba981c35c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175200 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{4}{4 + π}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175200 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175200 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd606c28-bab3-5cbd-8a07-6ba040325a99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175201 #edb/ref 1080 "The series is divergent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175201 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175201 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cdb8b45f-bf31-5954-9f4f-e885e74baf7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175202 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175202 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175202 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5da6aadb-a542-5e5e-8757-2157556219f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175203 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{π}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175203 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175203 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "66f7c05c-eeba-5618-820e-af1e62bbf928" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175806 #edb/ref 1069 "e-759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175806 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{(\\pi/3)^3}{3!} + \\dfrac{(\\pi/3)^5}{5!}-\\cdots + \\dfrac{(-1)^{n}(\\pi/3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+\\cdots\\,$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175806 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ffa8b1d-6651-594f-9c86-b4629d4cc2e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175806 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\sin x\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin x &= x - \\frac{x^{3}}{3!} + \\frac{x^{5}}{5!} - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}x^{2n + 1})/((2n + 1)!) + ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\ninto our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{3}) &= \\frac{π}{3} - ((π/3)^{3})/(3!) + ((π/3)^{5})/(5!) - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}(π/3)^{2n + 1})/((2n + 1)!) + ⋯ \\\\\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} &= \\frac{π}{3} - ((π/3)^{3})/(3!) + ((π/3)^{5})/(5!) - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}(π/3)^{2n + 1})/((2n + 1)!) + ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1069 "e-760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the sum $1 - \\dfrac{9}{2!} + \\dfrac{81}{4!}-\\cdots + \\dfrac{(-1)^{n}3^{2n}}{(2n)!} \\,\\cdots \\,$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b102c11-e930-5b11-805a-1ff11cdb5995" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175807 #edb/ref 1074 "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\cos x\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos x = 1 - \\frac{1}{2!}x^{2} + \\frac{1}{4!}x^{4} - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}x^{2n})/((2n)!) + ⋯\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (3) &= 1 - \\frac{3^{2}}{2!} + \\frac{3^{4}}{4!} - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}3^{2n})/((2n)!)⋯ \\\\\n\\cos (3) &= 1 - \\frac{9}{2!} + \\frac{81}{4!} - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}3^{2n})/((2n)!)⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\cos(3)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1039 "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Sine" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175950 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "a1e462d1-0add-520b-afbf-4c9b07970db4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175951 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175951 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175951 #edb/ref 1039 "Recognizing Series That Are Similar to the Maclaurin Expansion for Cosine" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175951 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175951 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ac85697c-557a-5b74-8046-79e9c345afc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186176693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1045 "Recognizing Standard Maclaurin Series for Trigonometric Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186176693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176122 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "5b617917-9881-594e-8972-61a82f2871a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176508 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186175186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176508 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50897" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176508 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $-2 + \\frac{8}{3!} - \\frac{32}{5!} + ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}(-2)^{2n + 1})/((2n + 1)!) + ⋯$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176508 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b610a1ae-13a4-52d6-8097-cd81c48ac52e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176510 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186175198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176510 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50935" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176510 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the sum of the series $\\frac{π}{4} - ((π/4)^{3})/(3!) + ((π/4)^{5})/(5!) - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}(π/4)^{2n + 1})/((2n + 1)!) + ⋯$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176510 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad9b9f3f-7dff-5b1d-aff9-251f7b31c672" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176676 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176676 #edb/ref 1061 2584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176676 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "02032486-ef93-5b31-a042-ff9aedc94caf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176676 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176677 #edb/ref 1061 2586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176677 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ded33c8c-6f4b-5349-ade4-f49fb9e69602" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176677 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186175951 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176693 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186176676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176693 #edb/ref 1061 32570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176693 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ed13fe45-d03c-55c5-912d-7530fab1d9cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176693 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186176979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176979 #edb/ref 1064 "We need to recognize when a particular series looks like a standard Maclaurin series. A list of some common Maclaurin series is given below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{1 - x} = 1 + x + x^{2} + ⋯ + x^{n} + ⋯ = ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)x^{n}, & x ∈ (-1, 1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{1 + x} = 1 - x + x^{2} - ⋯ + (-1)^{n}x^{n} + ⋯ = ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)(-1)^{n}x^{n}, & x ∈ (-1, 1) \\\\ e^{x} = 1 + x + \\frac{1}{2!}x^{2} + ⋯ + \\frac{x^{n}}{n!} + ⋯ = ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)\\frac{x^{n}}{n!}, & x ∈ (- ∞, ∞) \\\\ \\ln (1 + x) = x - \\frac{1}{2}x^{2} + \\frac{1}{3}x^{3} - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n + 1}x^{n})/(n) + ⋯ = ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)((-1)^{n + 1}x^{n})/(n), & x ∈ (-1, 1]; \\sin (x) = x - \\frac{1}{3!}x^{3} + \\frac{1}{5!}x^{5} + ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}x^{2n + 1})/((2n + 1)!) + ⋯ = ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)((-1)^{n}x^{2n + 1})/((2n + 1)!),\\begin{vmatrix}x ∈ (- ∞, ∞) \\\\ \\cos (x) = 1 - \\frac{1}{2!}x^{2} + \\frac{1}{4!}x^{4} - ⋯ + ((-1)^{n}x^{2n})/((2n)!) + ⋯ = ∑_(n = 0)^(∞)((-1)^{n}x^{2n})/((2n)!),\\end{vmatrix}x ∈ (- ∞, ∞)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this lesson, we will focus on recognizing the standard Maclaurin series for the sine and cosine functions.\n\n**Note:** To remember the series for $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$ easily, notice that they are both alternating series that contain every other term of the expansion for $e^x$. Sine has the odd-degree terms (since it is an odd function), and cosine has the even-degree terms (since it is an even function)." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176979 #edb/ref 1065 5193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176979 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d665f747-9ba7-5bcf-bb89-b9f7cf00815f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176979 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
